    <bpmn:process id="W_W4757" name="W4757. Loss Damage Waiver (LDW) Sale, Insurance Upsell &amp; Coverage Explanation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Deposit placed (W4756); standard counter upsell step
Frequency: Per rental
Volume: ~every rental (offer); ~40–70% take-rate benchmark
Owner: Rental Counter Associate / Rental Program (pricing W4748)
Participants: Customer, Risk &amp; Insurance (VS-26)
Source: workflow W4757 — Loss Damage Waiver (LDW) Sale, Insurance Upsell &amp; Coverage Explanation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4757_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4757_Lane1" name="Rental Counter Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4757_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4757_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4757_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4757_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4757_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4757_Start3" name="Deposit placed (W4756); standard counter upsell step">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4757_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4757_Task4" name="Offer the Loss Damage Waiver (LDW) and any supplementary covers (e.g…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Offer the Loss Damage Waiver (LDW) and any supplementary covers (e.g., cargo-cover for the customer&#x27;s load, tire-and-glass, personal-accident cover for the driver/passengers) per the W4748 product design; explain what each covers and the per-day fee
Responsible (R): Rental Counter Associate
Accountable (A): Rental Counter Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4757_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4757_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4757_Task5" name="not">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Clearly disclose what LDW is not (it is a waiver of the customer&#x27;s financial responsibility for damage/theft subject to terms — not insurance for the customer, and not cover for gross negligence, DUI (VS-150), unauthorized use, or geofence breach (W4749)); capture the customer&#x27;s accept/decline decision in the agreement (W4755)
Responsible (R): Rental Counter Associate / Risk
Accountable (A): Rental Counter Supervisor / Risk
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4757_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4757_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4757_Task6" name="Record the LDW election into the agreement &amp; billing (W4760); if declined…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Record the LDW election into the agreement &amp; billing (W4760); if declined, confirm the customer understands they remain liable up to the deductible via the deposit (W4756); the LDW take-rate &amp; loss-ratio feed the annual re-pricing (W4748)
Responsible (R): Rental Counter Associate
Accountable (A): Rental Counter Supervisor
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4757_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4757_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4757_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4757_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4757_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-717 (ensure controlled execution — Rental Transaction, Counter Operations &amp; Customer Onboarding (PA-162.2).) | - CTL-717: LDW offer with mandatory what-it-is-not disclosure; accept/decline recorded; take-rate/loss-ratio monitored (W4768)
Owner: Rental Counter Associate / Rental Program (pricing W4748)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4757_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4757_Annotation8" targetRef="W4757_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
