    <bpmn:process id="W_W4759" name="W4759. Return Inspection, Damage Assessment, Fuel/Cleaning Check &amp; Re-Release Gate" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vehicle returned to the lot
Frequency: Per rental
Volume: Every rental (~800–1,200/month)
Owner: Rental Counter Associate / Yard
Participants: Customer, Maintenance (W4750), LP (VS-23), Finance (W4760)
Source: workflow W4759 — Return Inspection, Damage Assessment, Fuel/Cleaning Check &amp; Re-Release Gate</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4759_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4759_Lane1" name="Rental Counter Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4759_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4759_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4759_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4759_Lane2" name="Yard">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4759_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4759_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4759_Start4" name="Vehicle returned to the lot">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4759_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4759_Task5" name="Capture the return baseline: odometer, fuel level, return date/time, telematics…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Capture the return baseline: odometer, fuel level, return date/time, telematics (W4749) stop; take a return condition photoset and diff against the checkout photoset (W4758); check for geofence/curfew breaches, harsh events, and unauthorized use (telematics)
Responsible (R): Rental Counter Associate / Yard
Accountable (A): Rental Counter Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4759_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4759_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4759_Task6" name="Assess damage (if any): triage new damage vs pre-existing, estimate repair cost…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Assess damage (if any): triage new damage vs pre-existing, estimate repair cost (links W4750/W4761), apply the LDW/deductible decision (W4757) — if LDW taken and terms met, waive customer cost; if declined, charge the deductible via the deposit (W4756); assess fuel-short (charge refuel fee), cleaning (charge cleaning fee if interior/soiled), late return (charge overtime), and excess mileage (per rate)
Responsible (R): Rental Counter Associate / Maintenance / Finance
Accountable (A): Rental Counter Supervisor / Finance
Duration: 5–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4759_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4759_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4759_Task7" name="Ground the vehicle for the between-rental safety check &amp; cleaning/refuel…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ground the vehicle for the between-rental safety check &amp; cleaning/refuel (W4750) before re-release; only re-release once safety-checked, refueled, cleaned, and CR/CTPL/insurance re-verified; this gate prevents releasing an unsafe/un-roadworthy vehicle to the next customer
Responsible (R): Yard / Maintenance
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Maintenance Lead
Duration: Per rental</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4759_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4759_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4759_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4759_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4759_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-94 (ensure rental fleet safety &amp; settlement integrity.) | - CTL-717: return photoset + telematics diff; damage/fuel/cleaning assessed and charged per terms; re-release only after safety check/refuel/clean
Owner: Rental Counter Associate / Yard</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4759_Assoc10" sourceRef="W4759_Annotation9" targetRef="W4759_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
