    <bpmn:process id="W_W4760" name="W4760. Rental Billing, Settlement, Deposit Release &amp; POS/Account Posting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Return inspection complete (W4759)
Frequency: Per rental
Volume: Every rental (~800–1,200/month)
Owner: Finance / Rental Counter (VS-17/VS-80)
Participants: Payment/Acquirer (VS-80), Finance (VS-17), Customer, BIR (e-invoicing VS-79)
Source: workflow W4760 — Rental Billing, Settlement, Deposit Release &amp; POS/Account Posting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4760_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4760_Lane1" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4760_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4760_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4760_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4760_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4760_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4760_Start3" name="Return inspection complete (W4759)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4760_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4760_Task4" name="Compute the final invoice from the rental record: base rate × time (W4758…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Compute the final invoice from the rental record: base rate × time (W4758 checkout → W4759 return), mileage (telematics W4749), LDW fee (W4757), fuel-short (W4759), cleaning/late/excess-mileage charges (W4759), and any damage/deductible (W4759); apply trade/loyalty discount (VS-13/VS-43) if eligible
Responsible (R): Finance / Rental Counter
Accountable (A): Rental Counter Supervisor / Finance
Duration: 3–6 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4760_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4760_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4760_Task5" name="Settle against the deposit hold (W4756): capture the final charge to the card…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Settle against the deposit hold (W4756): capture the final charge to the card and release the unused hold remainder, or collect/refund the cash difference (VS-08.2 controls); issue the BIR-compliant receipt / e-invoice (VS-79 W473 BIR EIS) for the rental revenue; post to GL (VS-17) as rental income + fuel-recovery + LDW income
Responsible (R): Finance / Rental Counter
Accountable (A): Finance
Duration: 3–6 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4760_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4760_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4760_Task6" name="Recon the daily rental batch to telematics records, deposit holds, and GL…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Recon the daily rental batch to telematics records, deposit holds, and GL postings; investigate variances (under-billed rentals, unreleased holds, unmatched cash); feed revenue/AR data to analytics (W4768) and finance close (VS-17.4)
Responsible (R): Finance
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4760_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4760_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4760_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4760_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4760_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-94 (ensure rental fleet safety &amp; settlement integrity.) | - CTL-717: final invoice from telematics; deposit capture/release per settlement; BIR e-invoice issued; daily batch recon
Owner: Finance / Rental Counter (VS-17/VS-80)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4760_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4760_Annotation8" targetRef="W4760_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
